{
  "101|Owl took the boy in as a foster son while having him trained (with the help of several co-mentors such as Lady Butterfly) to become a Shinobi [1]. Owl indoctrinated Sekiro with the Iron Code, which bids that \"Father is Absolute, and a master comes close second\" [1].": true,
  "102|The Mortal Blade is an odachi capable of slaying the undying, and its crimson blade will take the life of any who dares draw it [2]. Without the power of Resurrection, one could not hope to wield this weapon, which allows one to defeat even infested beings [2]. It is said that with it, you could kill one who cannot die through normal means, such as the infested [1]. The blade's true name is \"Gracious Gift of Tears,\" and it is required to draw Kuro's blood [2].": true,
  "103|In the Purification ending, Wolf \"proceeds to behead himself in order to sever the ties of immortality, freeing his Lord\" [1].": true,
  "104|Owl betrays Wolf because \"The Divine Heir's power... the Dragon's blood must be mine\" [3]. He orders Wolf to obey the Iron Code and forsake his master, stating \"As your father, I order you to forsake your master. From this moment, he is your master no more\" [3]. This betrayal stems from Owl's selfish goals of obtaining the Dragon's Blood after faking his own death [4].": true,
  "105|The Corrupted Monk guards the entrance to the Wedding Cave Door where the Shelter Stone is enshrined [2]. She also served as a guardian deity for the Mibu Village cave entrance [3].": true,
  "106|Dogen created the original prosthetic arm for the Sculptor [3]. The Sculptor later passed this invention on to Wolf, noting that \"When I lost my left arm, Dogen created that thing\" [2].": true,
  "107|Dragonrot spreads when one known to Wolf is coughing and wheezing, as it is likely they are afflicted with the sickness [1]. The disease manifests after Wolf perishes definitely four times, causing those without the power to become sick [3]. Repeated use of the Dragon's Heritage leads to stagnation, which eventually overflows and causes this condition [3].": false,
  "108|Emma created the gourd: \"The medicinal waters in this gourd spring forth on their own\" [2]. She confirmed her authorship when she stated, \"Yes. It was intended for Lord Kuro\" [2]. Additionally, lore notes that \"One of Dogen's apprentices, Emma, invented the Healing Gourd\" [3].": true,
  "109|My library doesn't cover that.": true,
  "110|My library doesn't cover that.": true
}